Department: Department of Computer Science, Koforidua Technical University
Date: August 2026

Abstract
This project designs, implements and evaluates a secure, scalable wireless campus network using Cisco Packet Tracer. The network supports multiple user groups across academic, administrative and residential areas, implementing VLAN segmentation, controller‑based WLAN (WLC + CAPWAP), WPA2‑Enterprise (802.1X) with RADIUS authentication, DHCP/DNS services, QoS for voice and video, guest captive portal, research lab isolation, and redundancy (HSRP, LACP, WLC HA). Simulation tests measure throughput, latency, jitter and authentication performance. Results demonstrate functional authentication workflows, VLAN isolation, prioritized voice/video traffic, and the viability of the design for campus deployment. Appendices contain full device configurations, test scripts, and instructions to reproduce the Packet Tracer topology.

